00:32:51.530 --> 00:32:55.130
So let's work out the example
for this particular setting,

00:32:55.130 --> 00:32:58.190
where let's say you had the
alphabets, which we have

00:32:58.190 --> 00:33:01.430
been discussing, 0, 1, 2,
and then your frequencies

00:33:01.430 --> 00:33:02.888
were 3, 3, 2.

00:33:02.888 --> 00:33:03.740
M is 8.

00:33:03.740 --> 00:33:05.990
Cumulative
probabilities is this.

00:33:05.990 --> 00:33:12.210
And so let's try to work out the
final encoding for 1, 0, 2, 1.

00:33:12.210 --> 00:33:13.800
So let's start.

00:33:13.800 --> 00:33:15.450
So your initial state--

00:33:15.450 --> 00:33:18.130
let me just see.

00:33:18.130 --> 00:33:18.630
Yeah.

00:33:18.630 --> 00:33:19.710
OK, let's just do it.

00:33:19.710 --> 00:33:23.520
So your initial state is 0.

00:33:23.520 --> 00:33:27.360
At next step, you want
to encode input 1.

00:33:27.360 --> 00:33:31.680
So your-- let me use the same
symbols, which are used here.

00:33:31.680 --> 00:33:34.200
So your initial state x is 0.

00:33:34.200 --> 00:33:37.410
S is symbol, x is the state.

00:33:37.410 --> 00:33:40.380
So in the first step,
let's just-- when

00:33:40.380 --> 00:33:43.740
you are trying to encode
1, so now you get symbol 1.

00:33:43.740 --> 00:33:45.900
And so let's just work
out the new state.

00:33:45.900 --> 00:33:50.850
So new state is going to be x
previous by frequency s, which

00:33:50.850 --> 00:33:57.450
is just 3, in this case,
times M plus cumulative of 1,

00:33:57.450 --> 00:34:06.620
which in our case is 3, plus x
previous modulus of frequency s.

00:34:06.620 --> 00:34:08.540
So just writing
down the operation

00:34:08.540 --> 00:34:12.687
not doing anything funky here,
just like literally reading

00:34:12.687 --> 00:34:15.020
all our symbols, which we
have formed, all our notations

00:34:15.020 --> 00:34:17.179
and just plugging it back.

00:34:17.179 --> 00:34:19.940
And so this gives your x as 3.

00:34:19.940 --> 00:34:23.510
So after step one,
your new status is 3.

00:34:23.510 --> 00:34:27.330
So step zero, step one.

00:34:27.330 --> 00:34:27.830
OK.

00:34:27.830 --> 00:34:29.120
Let's do step two now.

00:34:29.120 --> 00:34:31.820
So now the next symbol
you receive is 0.

00:34:31.820 --> 00:34:34.489
So your next symbol is 0.

00:34:34.489 --> 00:34:36.409
Now you start from
the previous state.

00:34:36.409 --> 00:34:42.110
So your previous state is 3
and your frequency is so far 0.

00:34:42.110 --> 00:34:45.650
Let's just-- for 0, I'm going
to pick the first element here.

00:34:50.570 --> 00:34:57.980
So for 0, the frequency is just
3 times 8 plus my cumul s is 0.

00:34:57.980 --> 00:35:03.120
And then again, it's 3
modulus 3, which is 0.

00:35:03.120 --> 00:35:08.340
So this is 1, this is just 0,
and so this gives your updated

00:35:08.340 --> 00:35:09.330
state to be 8.

00:35:12.430 --> 00:35:15.340
And then you can keep doing
this for each symbol, which

00:35:15.340 --> 00:35:16.180
is being added.

00:35:16.180 --> 00:35:19.630
So at each step, you are
updating the previous state

00:35:19.630 --> 00:35:21.835
based on the new symbol,
which is being received.

00:35:25.820 --> 00:35:26.320
OK.

00:35:26.320 --> 00:35:29.530
So I'm working this
out like for you,

00:35:29.530 --> 00:35:33.430
but we have this worked out in
the slides in the neater format,

00:35:33.430 --> 00:35:35.320
if you like that, but yeah.

00:35:35.320 --> 00:35:38.050
So this is just like going
through the same operations,

00:35:38.050 --> 00:35:42.580
which we discussed just
now like, just each step.

00:35:42.580 --> 00:35:46.420
And if you keep doing that,
in this case, you'll get 101,

00:35:46.420 --> 00:35:51.300
let's say, as the final
state which is being encoded.

00:35:51.300 --> 00:35:53.970
Before we go on,
we'll decode this,

00:35:53.970 --> 00:35:57.510
but let's try to see the same
formula for something which

00:35:57.510 --> 00:36:03.450
