00:36:48.880 --> 00:36:50.380
we have been seeing so far.

00:36:50.380 --> 00:36:57.210
This will lead down to x
previous times 10 plus s.

00:36:57.210 --> 00:37:01.350
So this is-- and that basically
would happen because--

00:37:01.350 --> 00:37:02.520
I'm giving away the answer.

00:37:02.520 --> 00:37:07.980
This will always be 0, this will
be s, and this by frequency s

00:37:07.980 --> 00:37:08.830
doesn't matter.

00:37:08.830 --> 00:37:12.260
So it's just multiplying by M.

00:37:12.260 --> 00:37:13.220
So I know this is fast.

00:37:13.220 --> 00:37:13.940
Just work it out.

00:37:13.940 --> 00:37:16.670
It's very basic divisions.

00:37:16.670 --> 00:37:19.340
So whatever this
beast looking thing

00:37:19.340 --> 00:37:23.810
we came up with, actually
in the simpler case,

00:37:23.810 --> 00:37:26.600
leads to the exact
same thing, which where

00:37:26.600 --> 00:37:27.815
we started our lecture from.

00:37:34.250 --> 00:37:35.960
OK.

00:37:35.960 --> 00:37:38.780
So far, so good, but now
we also have to figure out

00:37:38.780 --> 00:37:40.790
how to decode it uniquely.

00:37:40.790 --> 00:37:44.090
I haven't really told
